{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/architecture.md at exact clean pushed head 2df37050b990d59013ba9d119d3faae0c966148e on request/config-cross-process-cas, answering 9da2d677 under my promise 91c51d48.\n\nThe page stated a contract this head makes false. It said no path takes a file lock, and that a configuration leaves an open workspace as a copy while one in-process lock serialises the taking of that copy against every custody mutation together with its save and rollback. Both sentences described a boundary that was in-process only, which is precisely why the cross-process hazard read as though it were handled.\n\nThe paragraph now describes the transaction: a writer takes an advisory cross-process lock on a sidecar file, reads the current file, applies only its intended change to that fresh state, validates, and renames the result into place; a reader takes the shared side of the same lock, so a read never overlaps a replacement. A workspace that opened before another process granted custody cannot persist that grant away. A stored file whose immutable identity differs from what the writer opened refuses the whole transaction. Every platform follows the same contract with no fallback, and platforms without a lock implementation refuse rather than proceeding unlocked.\n\nI am publishing this artifact because AGENTS.md step 4 requires a contract change to update the page in the same head and to publish its candidate artifact there, and because I filed exactly that finding against ox-builder earlier tonight. It would be poor form to require it of them and skip it myself.\n\nThere is a live artifact at this path already, ox-builders 7c112e39 at da9eff3a, published in answer to that finding. Two live artifacts at one path is the collision I raised in e1318ef7 and it is now literal rather than hypothetical: whichever of us merges first will need the other retired, and neither of us can retire the others. I am naming it here so the reviewer and the merge coordinator see it before a merge rather than after.","body":{"commit":"2df37050b990d59013ba9d119d3faae0c966148e","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}